  "record": {
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "Root cause confirmed: the Shift-safe keypad helper deliberately polled each Numpad key together with its navigation twin, so physical Left/Right/Up/Down were treated as Numpad 4/6/8/2 and moved the camera. That union is removed. The installed editor now accepts only Numpad input with Num Lock on; Ctrl is the fine-step modifier, and the existing Shift-edge protection still prevents a stranded runaway key. Test physical arrows first: the camera must not move. Then use Num Lock-on Numpad 4/6 and 8/2: those must still adjust horizontal and distance.",
